//PAULA THE STRIPPER - DIALOGUES

// Greeting dialogues (random one plays when picked up)
{
	id: paula_greeting_a
	text: "Thanks for stopping. I needed to get out of that city for a while."
}

{
	id: paula_greeting_b
	text: "Where are you headed? I'm always up for a good road trip."
}

{
	id: paula_greeting_c
	text: "Sure, handsome. But fair warning: I'm better company when there's music."
}

// Initial hitch dialogue (longer conversation)
{
	id: paula_hitch
	text: "I'm Paula. Ten years under neon lights and now I'm on the road. Life is weird. But every mile gets me closer to my daughter."
}

// General conversation dialogue
{
	id: paula_talk
	text: "My ex has custody. But I'm going to win that fight. And for that I need money. A lot of money. That's why I'm out here on the road."
}

// Trust-building talks before Paula asks for help
{
	id: paula_trust_1
	text: "I don't usually tell this to just anyone. But with you I feel a little calmer. I guess spending so many hours on the road gets a girl talking."
}

{
	id: paula_trust_2
	text: "My daughter's name is Emma. She's seven. I miss her, but I know missing her isn't enough. I want to show her I can be there for her."
}

// First quest: get Paula a drink (completes on the spot, like June's coffee quest)
{
	id: paula_drink_complete
	text: "Oh, thank you. This takes the edge off my nerves. It's been years since anything scared me this much, and I've danced in front of anyone."
}

// Second quest: take Paula to the lawyer
{
	id: paula_begin_lawyer
	text: "I worked up the courage to ask around. There's a lawyer in a big city out east who can help me with custody. Would you take me there? For now I just need to get there."
}

{
	id: paula_lawyer_trip_complete
	text: "I talked to the lawyer. He says there's a chance of getting a custody agreement, but it's going to take time and I have to wait for his answer. Can I stay with you in the meantime? I've got nowhere to go, and traveling does me good."
}

// Second quest: Paula takes one last, well-paid stage job
{
	id: paula_request_fee
	text: "I got offered one last night of work at a club. It pays really well, and that way I'll be able to pay the lawyer. But it'll be the last time I ever do this. Will you take me?"
}

{
	id: paula_lawyer_fee_complete
	text: "They paid me really well. With this the lawyer can file the papers. And I mean it: I never want to do this again. That was my last night on stage. Now we wait; for the first time I feel like this could work."
}

// A couple of conversations pass before Paula gets the decision
{
	id: paula_case_wait
	text: "The lawyer says the case is going well, but these things don't get resolved overnight. I'm trying to be patient."
}

{
	id: paula_custody_news
	text: "She just called me. They signed the agreement: I got custody back. Emma is waiting at a stop far from the city. I can't believe I'm finally going to see her."
}

// Final quest: take Paula to her daughter
{
	id: paula_final_trip
	text: "Will you take me to her? I don't want to waste another minute. After all this time, I can't believe I'm going to hug her."
}

{
	id: paula_reunion_complete
	text: "Emma threw herself into my arms. I don't know how to thank you for all of this. I want you to keep my stage bustier; it was part of a life I've left behind. Now I want to look forward."
}

// Additional character-specific dialogues

{
	id: paula_impression_thinking
	text: "She looks out the window almost the whole time, but every time her phone buzzes, her face changes. Hope. Fear. And then determination again."
}

{
	id: paula_conversation_about_daughter
	text: "She's seven. Emma. God, I miss her so much. Some nights, on stage, I imagined she could see me and that one day she'd understand why I had to do this."
}

{
	id: paula_conversation_about_ex
	text: "He's not a bad guy. It's just... he wanted me to stop dancing and I wanted my freedom. We both thought we could make it work. We couldn't."
}

{
	id: paula_mention_future
	text: "When I get custody back, that's it. A new city, a new job, a new life. Something honest. Something that lets me be her mom every day."
}
